# CODEOWNERS — review routing for safety-critical paths
#
# GitHub uses this file to auto-request reviews when a PR touches a path.
# When combined with the "Require review from Code Owners" branch protection
# rule on dev/main, no PR touching these paths can merge without the listed
# owner's approval. That's the second half of layer 4 enforcement in the
# safety architecture (the first half is the gates.yml workflow).
#
# Format:  <pattern>  @user1 @user2 (or @org/team)
# Patterns are gitignore-style. Later matches override earlier ones.
#
# See docs/SAFETY_ARCHITECTURE.md for the full architecture.
# Task: gate-architecture-2026-05-26

# ── Default fallback: nothing required ─────────────────────────────────────
# (Listed paths below require Calvin specifically.)

